{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98744","id":2158907788,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6ArlGM","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98744","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98744.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98744.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98744","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98744/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98744/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98744/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/141737d168fa984fc410495e38ee308e8cd5c6a2","number":98744,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Docs: Standardize names and terms for renderers","user":{"login":"tetrapod00","id":145553014,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKz2dg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145553014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00","html_url":"https://github.com/tetrapod00","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Part of https://github.com/godotengine/godot-docs/issues/10139.\r\nSee also https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98747, https://github.com/godotengine/godot-docs/pull/10183.\r\n\r\nNew standards, for *user-facing docs*:\r\n- Godot has three *renderers* or *rendering methods*: **Forward+**, **Mobile**, and **Compatibility**. In most user-facing docs, these are referred to as \"renderers\". They are exposed by the engine as \"rendering methods\", and \"rendering method\" is a valid term to use.\r\n- Godot has four *rendering drivers*: **OpenGL**, **Vulkan**, **Direct3D 12**, **Metal**. \r\n- Godot has a rendering abstraction layer called \"RenderingDevice\". This can be referred to as the \"RenderingDevice backend\".\r\n- The term \"backend\" should be avoided in user-facing docs, as it is ambiguous. Especially the terms \"Compatibility backend\", \"Forward+ backend\", \"Vulkan backend\", are to be avoided.\r\n- The Forward+ renderer is called \"Forward+\". Avoid \"Forward Plus\" or \"forward_plus\" unless `+` is not a valid symbol.\r\n- The Mobile renderer is called \"Mobile\". Avoid \"Forward Mobile\". This rendering method is exposed in the project settings as \"mobile\" and referred to as \"Mobile\" in the engine interface.\r\n- The Compatibility renderer is called \"Compatibility\". Only use \"GL Compatibility\" when needed. For example, `gl_compatibility` is how it is exposed in the project settings.\r\n\r\nThis PR changes:\r\n- \"GL Compatibility\" to \"Compatibility\", since that is what shows up in the editor.\r\n- Ambiguous usages of \"backend\" are made explicit: they are either *renderers*, *rendering drivers*, or the *RenderingDevice backend*.\r\n- Existing references to \"rendering methods\" are left unchanged, since \"rendering method\" is still a valid term.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":283518839,